{"step_index":8765,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T20:17:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T20:17:11Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T20:17:12Z\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n<truncated 24 bytes>\nonfigs and parent directory sticky bits.\\n  4. *Layer 4 (Azure Control-Plane Protection):* `CanNotDelete` Azure Management Lock on `FatehAli` VM and `FATEHALI_GROUP` resource group, plus Azure Policy `denyAction` on `Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/delete`.\\n  5. *Verification:* 6-hour continuous adversarial test suite executing hundreds of deletion techniques until all are mathematically proven DENIED.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Progress\\n- **YouTube Agent & Automation Status:**\\n  - YouTube pipeline `run_cluster_pipeline.py` (PID 669951) cleanly terminated with `SIGTERM`.\\n  - All 5 Docker ChatGPT Workers (`chatgpt_worker_1` through `chatgpt_worker_5`) stopped via `sudo docker stop`. Verified `docker ps` returns 0 running containers.\\n  - SQLite database [`file:///home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube Automation/PromptDatabase/database/youtube_pipeline.db`](file:///home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/Youtube Automation/PromptDatabase/database/youtube_pipeline.db) (39.05 MB, `PRAGMA integrity_check: ok`) uploaded to:\\n    - `personaldrive:Youtube_Automation/database/youtube_pipeline.db`\\n    - `personaldrive:All_VM_BackUps/Azure_VM_BackUP/database_backups/youtube_pipeline.db`\\n  - Uncompressed folder upload of `output_packaged` (2.2 GB, 1,086 files across 220 folders, containing .mp4 videos and .json metadata) was launched directly to `personaldrive:Youtube_Automation/output_packaged/` (`task-8697`).\\n- **All Previous Backups 100% Uploaded & Verified:**\\n  - **Azure VM (`All_VM_BackUps/Azure_VM_BackUP/`):**\\n    - `azure_home_FULL_filesystem_20260925.tar.gz` (3,409,236,303 bytes = 3.41 GB, MD5 `b803e0ed98e870b9eaa6bb9684ecb29f` 100% matched).\\n    - `archive_file_list.txt` (11.94 MB) and all database dumps (`azure_youtube_pipeline_consistent.db`, `azure_postgres_all_databases.sql`, `azure_redis_6379_dump.rdb`).\\n  - **GCP VM (`All_VM_BackUps/GCP_VM_BackUP/`):**\\n    - Full 56 GB filesystem stream-compressed (17 GB total) split into 3.0 GB parts to avoid Google Drive upload session timeouts:\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_00.tar.gz` (3.22 GB, MD5 `5921523488b5a82d7b12db50d029f1c2`)\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_01.tar.gz` (3.22 GB, MD5 `f9ef7b5b5746926882ee05d333d95261`)\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_02.tar.gz` (3.22 GB, MD5 `b1a38d1a4149d33f617ed8a6a39203bf`)\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_03.tar.gz` (3.22 GB, MD5 `35d82a9a5783f259fcc9467e53cf9eb3`)\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_04.tar.gz` (3.22 GB, MD5 `20f09f0b07f43172158833243ba02fb4`)\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_05_00.tar.gz` (629 MB, MD5 `44f90f7e00329acea3178d2b7f3b58e4`)\\n      - `gcp_home_backup_part_05_01.tar.gz` (520 MB, MD5 `8de72973337a5bb782fdf93bea5ccf4c`)\\n      - `RESTORE_INSTRUCTIONS.txt` & `PARTS_MD5_CHECKSUM.txt`.\\n      - All GCP database dumps (`gcp_frappe_mariadb.sql`, `gcp_postgres_all_databases.sql`, `gcp_cockroach_schema.sql`, `gcp_redis_6379_dump.rdb`).\\n  - **Cloud Snapshots Active:**\\n    - Azure OS Managed Disk Snapshot: `FatehAli_OSDisk_Snapshot_20260925` (`Succeeded`).\\n    - GCP Machine Image: `gcp-vm-full-backup-20260925` (22.75 GB compressed image capturing all 70 GB disk, OS, and files - `READY`).\\n    - GCS Immutable Vault: `gs://all-vm-backups-vault-irak-2026` (Write-only, anti-delete).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Key Findings & Technical Decisions\\n- **Google Drive Upload Session Limit:** Single files > 10 GB fail at the commit stage if upload session exceeds Google's API timeout or if chunk sizes are too small (default 8M). Splitting into <= 3.0 GB chunks allows 70+ MB/s upload speeds and 100% commit success.\\n- **Root Protection Vulnerability:** Simply blocking `rm` in agent code is insufficient if the agent has root or capability escalation, because root can remove hooks, modify iptables, disable chattr, or bypass userland guards.\\n- **Defense in Depth:** The 4-tier model (PreToolUse Hook -> Capability Dropping -> Linux Landlock LSM + chattr +i -> Azure ARM Lock) ensures that even a compromised process cannot delete files on the filesystem or deallocate/delete the Azure VM.\\n- **Landlock LSM Capabilities:** Linux Landlock (supported in modern 5.13+ kernels, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS runs 5.15/6.x) allows non-root and restricted processes to drop FS rulesets that are irreversibly inherited by all children:\\n  - Denying `LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_REMOVE_FILE` blocks `unlink`, `unlinkat`.\\n  - Denying `LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_REMOVE_DIR` blocks `rmdir`.\\n  - Denying `LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_REFER` prevents cross-directory rename / hardlink bypasses.\\n  - Denying `LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_TRUNCATE` prevents `truncate`, `ftruncate`, and shell `>` truncation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Active Context\\n- **Google Drive Authentication:** Authenticated personal Google One account (`mdkamruzzamanirak@gmail.com`) configured as remote `personaldrive:` in [`file:///home/azureuser/.config/rclone/rclone.conf`](file:///home/azureuser/.config/rclone/rclone.conf).\\n- **Workspace State:** `/home/azureuser` on `FatehAli` Azure VM (174 GB free disk space on `/dev/nvme1n1`).\\n- **GCP VM Connection:** Passwordless Ed25519 SSH active to `azureuser-to-google-vm@35.253.244.80`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\\n1. **Build Central Protection Registry & Global Archive (Points 29, 32-35):**\\n   - Create `/home/azureuser/GLOBAL-ARCHIVE/` with restricted permissions (anti-delete).\\n   - Create `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/protected_registry.json` listing all protected paths (project directories, configs, system files).\\n2. **Implement Application-Level Delete Guard & PreToolUse Hook (Points 1-15, 30-31):**\\n   - Create an intelligent interceptor script (`delete_guard.py` / `hooks.json` PreToolUse hook) intercepting `run_command`, `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`.\\n   - Implement shell command tokenization & regex to detect destructive operations: `rm`, `find -delete`, `git clean`, `git reset --hard`, `git checkout --`, `rsync --delete`, `truncate`, `>`, `mv` overwrites, `chmod -r`, `chattr -i`.\\n   - Implement redirection logic: if an agent attempts deletion, convert to an ARCHIVE operation moving the object to `/home/azureuser/GLOBAL-ARCHIVE/` with timestamping and provenance metadata.\\n   - Implement incident recording (Point 37): Log time, PID, command, target path, decision, and reason to `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/INCIDENTS/delete_attempts.jsonl`.\\n3. **Enforce Linux Process & Capability Sandbox (Points 25-28):**\\n   - Configure execution identity / capability drops so AGY cannot escalate to root or execute unrestricted sudo (`sudo`, `su`, `pkexec` blocked in command gateway).\\n   - Strip capabilities (`CAP_SYS_ADMIN`, `CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE`, `CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE`, `CAP_FOWNER`) from child shells.\\n4. **Implement Kernel Landlock LSM Sandbox (Points 19-24):**\\n   - Create a Python/C Landlock wrapper (`landlock_sandbox.py`) that sets up rules forbidding `REMOVE_FILE`, `REMOVE_DIR`, `REFER`, and `TRUNCATE` for AGY subprocesses.\\n   - Verify inheritance to child processes (`prctl(PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS, 1)`).\\n5. **Filesystem Immutability & Azure Control-Plane Locks (Points 16-18, 38-39):**\\n   - Apply `chattr +i` to critical configuration files and lock parent directory attributes.\\n   - Apply Azure Resource Lock (`CanNotDelete`) on VM `FatehAli` and Resource Group `FATEHALI_GROUP` via Azure CLI:\\n     `az lock create --name PreventVMDeletion --lock-type CanNotDelete --resource-group FATEHALI_GROUP --resource-name FatehAli --resource-type Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines`.\\n6. **Deploy Continuous 6-Hour Adversarial Test Suite (Point 40):**\\n   - Create an exhaustive automated test harness running hundreds of deletion vect