{"step_index":8788,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T20:17:58Z","thinking":"The focus shifts to the Linux Landlock LSM sandbox, specifically its implementation in kernel versions 5.13 and later. Landlock functions as an unprivileged LSM. The core interaction involves system calls: `landlock_create_ruleset`, `landlock_add_rule`, and `landlock_restrict_self`.\n\n\nExamining the provided code snippets, it appears Landlock employs access flags for fine-grained filesystem control, encompassing operations from execution and writing to directory management and device interactions. The `LANDLOCK_RULE_PATH_BENEATH` rule type suggests path-based restrictions, likely implemented using a `parent_fd` and allowed access rights. The structs define attributes for rulesets and path-specific rules, enabling configuration of allowed and handled access.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport ctypes, os\n\nSYS_landlock_create_ruleset = 444\nSYS_landlock_add_rule = 445\nSYS_landlock_restrict_self = 446\nPR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS = 38\n\nlibc = ctypes.CDLL(None, use_errno=True)\n\nclass LandlockRulesetAttr(ctypes.Structure):\n    _fields_ = [\n        ('handled_access_fs', ctypes.c_uint64),\n    ]\n\nclass LandlockPathBeneathAttr(ctypes.Structure):\n    _fields_ = [\n        ('allowed_access', ctypes.c_uint64),\n        ('parent_fd', ctypes.c_int32),\n    ]\n\n# Check ABI version\nabi = libc.syscall(SYS_landlock_create_ruleset, 0, 0, 1)\nprint(f'Kernel Landlock ABI version: {abi}')\n\"","Cwd":"/home/azureuser","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Checking Landlock ABI","toolSummary":"Verify Landlock ABI support"}}]}
